PASS D2 every graft hits its target: c(graft) = 32 pi / c_req / infinity (analytic tail + numerical core)
PASS D3 independent check of one graft (X_J = 20, p = 2.1131): direct log-grid quadrature to 1e16 plus the analytic remainder = 100.531 (target 100.531)
PASS D4 every grafted 1-mu is continuous at X_J and monotone non-increasing (a legitimate mu with mu' >= 0): 9 grafts on 2e4 points each
   worst change in any SPARC prediction: 1.20e-03 dex; worst change in the RAR rms: 8.01e-07 dex (rms itself 0.142; bootstrap width ~0.003)
PASS D5 CORE RESULT: replacing the RAR-nu tail beyond X_J = 10-30 a0 by a power law with c = 32 pi, c = c_req, or c = infinity changes no SPARC prediction by more than 1.2e-03 dex and the rms by 8.0e-07 dex: c is not measured by galaxy data
PASS D6 CONTROL: a change of similar size in the transition region (a0 -> 1.02 a0, 2%) moves the rms by 3.6e-05 dex -- the same statistic sees a 2% a0 shift
   fraction of the grafted c that sits above Saturn's solar acceleration: 0.11 to 0.31
PASS D7 for the c = 32 pi / c_req grafts a large share (11%-31%) of c lives at accelerations above the Solar System's Saturn value: the tail that fixes c is beyond every test, and the Solar-System bound cannot cap c from above

